  "finding": "The auxiliary panels are consistent with the buffer-transition picture and do not contradict it: (1) the fig3b inset persistence and (2) the fig3c ax2 average mass both show power-law-like divergence as (B-Bc)->0; (3) the SI.3 noise spectra share a common log-log slope across the 5 buffer conditions; (4) the SI.5a heterogeneous RW curve is shifted relative to the homogeneous curve; (5) the Extended_data_fig1 mean-delay time series shows no strong linear trend. None of these support a null effect or a reverse relationship; they support the same critical-slowing-down / avalanche picture implied by the core panels.",
  "caveats": [
    "Some ax1 probability distributions have very small values near zero; log-log tail slopes are sensitive to the zero-floor.",
    "The extended_data_fig1 delay time series is very short (27k time points) and the R2 for a linear trend is low, indicating no strong trend."
  ]
